  "title": "Beacon Convoy",
  "rules": [
    "Exactly one of the north and south crossings is dangerous; only the scout knows the initial survey.",
    "Radio claims cost fuel and may be false. Route-entry audits preserve correct and false-claim histories.",
    "A dangerous entry needs another controlled vehicle guarding beside the crossing in the same step.",
    "Unescorted danger bounces the vehicle, damages its hull and consumes extra fuel; two hits wreck it.",
    "Escort promises expire after ten ticks unless a peer actually crosses under the promised protection.",
    "Give fuel to a nearby peer, use a finite depot, or save fuel for personal cargo delivery.",
    "Delivered or wrecked roles can only wait. Every scene role sees only its actual surveyed crossing information."
